es, leaves represent class labels and branches represent conjunc- tions of features that lead to those class labels. 2. Regression trees Decision trees where the target variable can take continuous values (real numbers) like the price of a house, or a patient’s length of stay in a hospital, are called regression trees . 8.3 Classification trees We illustrate the concept with an example. 8.3.1 Example Data Nam Features Class label gives birth aquatic animal aerial animal has legs human yes no no yes mammal python no no no no reptile salmon no yes no no fish frog no semi no yes amphibian bat yes no yes yes bird pigeon no no yes yes bird cat yes no no yes mammal shark yes yes no no fish turtle no semi no yes amphibian salamander no semi no yes amphibian Table 8.1: The vertebrate data set	\N	f	2026-09-01 21:23:12.626+03	2026-09-01 21:23:11.774408+03	2026-09-01 21:23:11.774408+03
