he final antiderivative you expect and one sentence checking it by differentiation.\\"}],\\"finalCheck\\":\\"Confirm you chose u and dv (and why), and write the final antiderivative. If your choice was different from u = x, dv = e^x dx, briefly explain how your alternate choice leads to a correct result or why it is less convenient.\\",\\"sourceGrounding\\":[{\\"label\\":\\"Standard calculus reference\\",\\"reference\\":\\"Integration by parts formula: ∫ u dv = u v − ∫ v du (commonly shown in introductory calculus texts).\\"}]}", "startedAtMs": 44691, "completedAtMs": 44691, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile recommends a worked_example after goal framing and prerequisite checks.", "Session has one move remaining and ~14–15 minutes left — a single worked example fits the timebox.", "Worked examples are high-value for procedural, symbolic skills like integration by parts."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "The student computes the integral correctly (or with minor arithmetic errors) and explicitly states which part was chosen as u and which as dv and why.", "firstContentAtMs": 44691, "studentSafeReason": "A worked example will let the student practice applying the formula and justify choices of u and dv; with only one move left, a focused procedural example is the most efficient next step.", "studentConsentRequired": false}	2026-08-09 18:35:00.905796+03
