\\",\\"label\\":\\"releases (by-product)\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"co2\\",\\"to\\":\\"glucose\\",\\"label\\":\\"carbon atoms become part of\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"h2o\\",\\"to\\":\\"oxygen\\",\\"label\\":\\"source of O atoms released as\\"}],\\"altText\\":\\"Editable concept map showing light, CO2 and H2O as inputs to the chloroplast. Light supplies energy; chloroplast assembles glucose and releases oxygen. Arrows label inputs, energy flow, and products.\\",\\"editable\\":true,\\"fallbackText\\":\\"Concept map: Inputs — Light (energy), CO2 (carbon source), H2O (hydrogen/electrons). Central node: Chloroplast (site of photosynthesis). Outputs — Glucose (assembled from CO2 + H2O using light energy) and Oxygen (released when water is split). Edges label energy supply, inputs, product formation, and by-product release.\\"}", "startedAtMs": 51385, "completedAtMs": 51385, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile ranks visual representations (diagram) highly for Photosynthesis.", "Learner already completed misconception-demolition and goal framing; a diagram is the next recommended move in the opening->practice pattern.", "Remaining time and moves are limited — choose a concise, editable diagram activity to elicit evidence of understanding.", "Diagrams suit the low-mathematical, high-visual nature of the target concept."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Learner fills or edits the concept map to show CO2 and H2O as inputs, light as the energy source, and glucose (and O2) as products, and indicates the rough relationship (light energy used to assemble glucose from CO2 + H2O).", "firstContentAtMs": 51385, "studentSafeReason": "A visual representation helps consolidate the learner's corrected model after the misconception correction and goal framing; it's low-cost and matches the topic's high visual weight.", "studentConsentRequired": false}	2026-08-09 18:35:00.905796+03
