ned into organized action.\\"}],\\"takeaway\\":\\"Sequence: long‑standing social inequality set the moral grievance, economic collapse made suffering immediate, political failure shut down peaceful reform, and Enlightenment ideas provided the framework to turn grievance into revolution.\\"}", "startedAtMs": 25594, "completedAtMs": 25594, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile recommends starting with a story after goal framing", "Session type: repair — provide a clear, corrected narrative to replace gaps", "Short time remaining — use a concise, focused story (4 events) to cover main causes", "Follow-up checks (contrast_case, recall_check) are available in remaining moves"], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Student can list or paraphrase the main causes (e.g., social inequality, economic crisis, political dysfunction, Enlightenment ideas) and place them in a short sequence or explain one cause's role.", "firstContentAtMs": 25594, "studentSafeReason": "A brief narrative (story) will reconnect key factual causes in an organised, memorable sequence appropriate for repair work.", "studentConsentRequired": false}	2026-08-09 18:35:00.905796+03
