s).\\"}", "startedAtMs": 45599, "completedAtMs": 45599, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile recommends contrast_case after the story in the practicePattern.", "Learner persona 'repeated_struggle' benefits from focused comparisons that surface distinguishing features.", "Only one move remaining — a single targeted contrast case provides high value practice and diagnostic information.", "Low misconception richness means a contrast will be concise and unlikely to introduce confusion."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Learner explains (1–2 sentences) which of two short micro-scenarios from the contrast exemplifies a key cause (e.g., fiscal crisis vs. political exclusion) and justifies their choice by naming the distinguishing feature.", "firstContentAtMs": 45599, "studentSafeReason": "Contrast case is safe and appropriate: it helps the learner distinguish similar causes and apply reasoning after the story, fits the topic profile's recommended practice pattern, and uses low prerequisite density so no new background is required.", "studentConsentRequired": false}	2026-08-09 18:35:00.905796+03
