lants get their food from the soil, or do they make it themselves using light? Reply briefly with either \\\\\\"soil\\\\\\" or \\\\\\"make it\\\\\\".\\",\\"correction\\":\\"Plants do not take finished food from the soil. In photosynthesis, they use light energy to assemble glucose from carbon dioxide (from air) and water — the soil supplies water and mineral nutrients, but not the plant's carbon-based 'food'.\\",\\"evidence\\":[\\"Plants produce glucose in their leaves by combining CO2 + H2O using light energy (this is photosynthesis).\\",\\"Soil supplies minerals and water, which support growth, but it does not provide the carbon that becomes the plant’s sugar.\\"]}", "startedAtMs": 14640, "completedAtMs": 14640, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile flags a high-value misconception ('soil-food') that often causes repeated struggle.", "Session type is revision with limited moves — prioritize a focused corrective move.", "Recommended opening pattern for this topic begins with misconception_demolition."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Learner explicitly rejects the 'plants take food from soil' idea and explains (in their own words) that plants use light energy to assemble glucose from carbon dioxide and water, or correctly identifies one clear contradiction with the soil-food idea.", "firstContentAtMs": 14640, "studentSafeReason": "Student has a known misconception that directly blocks understanding; confronting it gently is safe and helpful.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_2_302ef691", "type": "goal_frame", "phase": "opening", "title": "Set a short application goal for Photosynthesis", "blockId": "live_block_2_93854d58", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Set a short application goal for Photosynthesis\\",\\"type\\":\\"goal_frame\\",\\"goal\\":\\"In one sentence, state a small, task-oriented goal using the corrected model (for example: “I will explain how plants make glucos