ifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Learner explicitly rejects the 'plants take food from soil' idea and explains (in their own words) that plants use light energy to assemble glucose from carbon dioxide and water, or correctly identifies one clear contradiction with the soil-food idea.", "firstContentAtMs": 14640, "studentSafeReason": "Student has a known misconception that directly blocks understanding; confronting it gently is safe and helpful.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_2_302ef691", "type": "goal_frame", "phase": "opening", "title": "Set a short application goal for Photosynthesis", "blockId": "live_block_2_93854d58", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Set a short application goal for Photosynthesis\\",\\"type\\":\\"goal_frame\\",\\"goal\\":\\"In one sentence, state a small, task-oriented goal using the corrected model (for example: “I will explain how plants make glucose from light, CO2 and H2O”) and agree to try a single short application (e.g., label which inputs are needed in a simple scenario).\\",\\"timeEstimateMinutes\\":5,\\"checkpoints\\":[\\"Write a one-sentence goal that uses light, carbon dioxide and water correctly.\\",\\"Complete a single short application task (label inputs or choose the correct inputs in a brief scenario).\\",\\"Briefly confirm whether the attempted application matched your goal and note any remaining confusion.\\"]}", "startedAtMs": 28300, "completedAtMs": 28300, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile's openingPattern recommends goal_frame after misconception_demolition.", "Session is time-limited with only two moves remaining — prefer a concise, high-value framing move.", "A short application check will produce clear evidence for readiness before a diagram/layered explanation."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Learner restates a clear, task-oriented goal (one sentence) such as 'I will explain how plants get glucose using light, CO2 and H2O' and agrees to try a single short application (e.g., label which inputs are needed for photosynthesis in a simple scenario).", "firstContentAtMs": 28300, "studentSafeReason": "After correcting the soil-food misconception, a brief goal frame focuses the learner on a small application task that reveals whether they can use the corrected idea safely and productively.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_3_01dca176", "type": "diagram", "phase": "explaining", "title": "Photosynthesis concept map — inputs, process, outputs", "blockId": "live_block_3_5162b625", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Photosynthesis concept map — inputs, process, outputs\\",\\"type\\":\\"diagram\\",\\"diagramType\\":\\"concept_map\\",\\"nodes\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"light\\",\\"label\\":\\"Light (energy)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Sunlight providing energy for the light reactions.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"co2\\",\\"label\\":\\"Carbon dioxide (CO2)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Taken from air through leaf stomata; carbon source for glucose.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"h2o\\",\\"label\\":\\"Water (H2O)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Taken up by roots; supplies electrons/H to reactions and O atoms.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"chloroplast\\",\\"label\\":\\"Chloroplast (site)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Cell organelle where light reactions and the Calvin cycle occur.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"light_reactions\\",\\"label\\":\\"Light reactions\\",\\"description\\":\\"Use light to make ATP and NADPH and split water (release O2).\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"calvin_cycle\\",\\"label\\":\\"Calvin cycle (carbon fixation)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Uses ATP and NADPH to assemble CO2 and H into glucose.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"glucose\\",\\"label\\":\\"Glucose (C6H12O6)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Organic product used for energy and growth.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"oxygen\\",\\"label\\":\\"Oxygen (O2)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Byproduct released when water is split.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"photosynthesis_process\\",\\"label\\":\\"Photosynthesis (o