ontinue\\",\\"type\\":\\"hook\\",\\"prompt\\":\\"Before I share a short illustrative story about the causes of the French Revolution, please type one sentence saying what you want to be able to do or understand (for example: “I want to be able to list and explain three main causes of the French Revolution”).\\",\\"reveal\\":\\"Thanks — now a brief story to make the main causes memorable: In the years before 1789, many French peasants and city workers struggled to pay heavy taxes while nobles and clergy lived comfortably. At the same time, the king’s government was nearly bankrupt after costly wars and poor tax systems, leaving food prices high and wages low. Enlightenment ideas about liberty and equality spread among educated Parisians, who began to question the old social order. Those three forces — popular hardship and inequality, fiscal crisis and government weakness, and the spread of revolutionary ideas — combined and ignited the uprising that became the French Revolution.\\",\\"anchor\\":\\"Will you commit to one sentence now?\\"}", "startedAtMs": 25038, "completedAtMs": 25038, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Session is a repair: require a cheap verbal commitment before proceeding", "Topic profile and prior move requested a student goal commitment", "Short, direct prompt will re-align focus quickly within time budget"], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Student types a one-sentence learning-goal or affirmation (e.g., 'I want to be able to list and explain three main causes of the French Revolution').", "firstContentAtMs": 25038, "studentSafeReason": "Asking for a brief student commitment is low-stakes and appropriate for secondary-level history instruction.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_3_2e80a3d3", "type": "story", "phase": "explaining", "title": "Brief vignette on causes of the French Revolution", "blockId": "live_block_3_0ac3b2ee", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Brief vignette on causes of the French Revolution\\",\\"type\\":\\"story\\",\\"setup\\":\\"A short, third-person vignette showing how social inequality, economic strain, and political failure combined to spark unrest in late-18th-century France.\\",\\"events\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"e1\\",\\"label\\":\\"Social strain among the people\\",\\"detail\\":\\"In a small village, a peasant family works dawn to dusk while nobles attend festivals; the villagers pay heavy rents and see no chance to improve their lives, breeding resentment toward the privileged classes.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"e2\\",\\"label\\":\\"Economic pressure and hardship\\",\\"detail\\":\\"In the market town, bread prices spike after a bad harvest and the government borrows heavily to cover royal debts; merchants and artisans face falling demand while taxes fall mostly on commoners, deepening anger and suffering.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"e3\\",\\"label\\":\\"Political breakdown at the center\\",\\"detail\\":\\"In Paris, reform-minded representatives fail to persuade the king and court to change taxation and representation; when the Estates-General meets, commoners demand a stronger voice and many conclude that the old political system cannot fix urgent social and economic problems.\\"}],\\"takeaway\\":\\"These three linked causes—deep social inequality, severe economic strain, and a political system that blocked effective reform—together helped trigger the French Revolution. In one sentence, name which of these causes you think was most important and why.\\"}", "startedAtMs": 40706, "completedAtMs": 40706, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile recommends a story as the next move after goal framing", "Session is repair-oriented — a concise story can quickly re-anchor misconceptions", "One move remaining in the time budget; a short story fits the remaining time", "Every new teaching target requires a cheap commitment first (ensure the student is ready to continue)"], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Stud