 "Safe to proceed: introductory framing to focus on key causes and align expectations.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_2_898eb7b8", "type": "story", "phase": "explaining", "title": "A Parisian family's view: causes of the French Revolution", "blockId": "live_block_2_3cd1b7ab", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"A Parisian family's view: causes of the French Revolution\\",\\"type\\":\\"story\\",\\"setup\\":\\"A short first-person vignette from the perspective of Jeanne, a member of a working-class Parisian family in the 1780s, showing daily life strained by rising prices, heavy taxes, and lack of political voice.\\",\\"events\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"e1\\",\\"label\\":\\"Empty bread basket\\",\\"detail\\":\\"I wake to find our bread ration smaller than last week. Flour prices have jumped and my husband's wages can't keep up, so we skip meals and worry each day about feeding the children.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"e2\\",\\"label\\":\\"Crushing taxes\\",\\"detail\\":\\"A tax collector passes through and demands more than before. The nobles and clergy seem exempt, while we pay again and again. I resent that money leaves our pocket but brings no relief.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"e3\\",\\"label\\":\\"No voice at the town meeting\\",\\"detail\\":\\"At the local meeting I try to raise our problems, but only the wealthy landowners are invited to decide taxes and laws. My words are ignored—we have no seat where decisions are made.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"e4\\",\\"label\\":\\"Rumors and anger spread\\",\\"detail\\":\\"Neighbors talk of hunger, of debts, and of how others live tax-free. People gather in the square, angry and ready to demand change; I feel fear, but also a fierce hope that things must be fixed.\\"}],\\"takeaway\\":\\"Jeanne's story highlights three key causes often linked to the French Revolution: severe economic hardship for ordinary people, an unfair and heavy tax burden largely borne by the commoners, and political exclusion from deci