, "completed": true}, "interactionState": {"revealed": true}}, {"id": "9066943d-6de9-4e29-bc8b-aac336a1aa3e", "status": "completed", "content": {"type": "hook", "title": "Recall Check: Why Agents Learn", "anchor": "Pages 1–3 — Reasons for Agent Learning", "prompt": "According to the uploaded notes on pages 1–3, what are the three main reasons we want an agent to learn rather than having designers program every improvement directly?", "reveal": "The three reasons from page 1 are: (1) designers cannot anticipate all possible situations (like a robot navigating a new maze), (2) designers cannot anticipate changes over time (like a stock market shifting from boom to bust), and (3) sometimes human programmers have no idea how to program a solution themselves (like recognizing family faces).", "schemaVersion": "petros.render.v2"}, "version": 1, "whyThis": "A recall check follows the hook and explanation to verify the learner's understanding of the document's reasons for agent learning.", "delivery": "ai", "sequence": 4, "createdAt": "2026-09-01T19:39:54.862Z", "questions": [], "sessionId": "668cc0e9-85cf-4dd4-b915-542656c986dc", "decisionId": "a92b27a8-ff34-43bc-bec1-2f03aa46701a", "completedAt": "2026-09-01T19:40:16.197Z", "correlationId": "cb0a4744-f595-46f7-8ff7-e2d942379f41", "observedOutcome": {"stage": 3, "completed": true}, "interactionState": {"revealed": true, "noteArtifactId": "85f29f24-b028-4701-b136-e8564264bf9f", "requestedAction": "note_saved", "flashcardArtifactId": "892197c0-a98a-4511-9e72-33d83e0b11d8"}}, {"id": "8a7e2827-0cd5-4a0d-8186-a8cb59edbb0b", "status": "completed", "content": {"type": "synthesis", "title": "Synthesizing Pages 1–3", "prompt": "In one clear sentence, summarize why machine learning agents need to learn from examples rather than relying entirely on hard-coded human programming, as outlined on pages 1–3.", "forwardLink": "Next, we will explore Forms of Learning and Supervised Learning in greater depth.", "schemaVersion": "petros.rende