 want an agent to learn? If the design of the agent can be improved, why wouldn’t the designers just program in that improvement to begin wit h? • There are three main reasons. • First, the designers cannot anticipate all possible situations that the agent might find itself in. For example, a robot designed to navigate mazes must learn the layout of each new maze it encounters. • Second, the design ers cannot anticipate all changes over time; a program designed to predict tomorrow’s stock market prices must learn to adapt when conditions change from boom to bust. • Third, sometimes human programmers have no idea how to program a solution themselves. F or example, most people are good at recognizing the faces of family members, but even the best programmers are unable to progra", "section": "Pages 1–3", "version": "1:46b63aeb22c661ff", "sourceId": "136cd389-8be9-4f12-937f-8bcbc5acf96a", "sourceType": "document"}], "pageIndex": 0, "returnHref": "/materials", "referenceId": "136cd389-8be9-4f12-937f-8bcbc5acf96a", "resumeToken": "7f58aab8-a30f-4b4f-a891-892a5fc8f20c", "returnLabel": "Study materials", "registerFactors": ["The student explicitly asked to be taught from their own uploaded pages.", "Keep source grounding visible and separate explanation from quotation."], "emotionalRegister": "curious_grounded", "policyDisclosures": ["Petros uses only extracted pages available to this student and cites their page numbers.", "Document teaching is for explanation and limited quotation; the original file remains the source."], "sourceFingerprint": "1c2d133496a680102f7c074632fdda9a7075613e061891c76891c2abbdbbb1af", "institutionalDecision": {"homework": null, "syllabus": {"decision": "within_bounds", "allowedDepth": 3, "teachingShape": "normal", "requestedTopic": "Pages 1–3", "sourceBoundary": {"approvedSourceIds": [], "externalSourcesAllowed": false}, "studentMessage": "This topic is inside your institution's approved learning scope."}}}, "elapsedSeconds": 127, "fallbackNotice