ure important patterns. A perfectly fit decision tree performs well for training data but performs poorly for unseen test data. If the decision tree is allowed to train to its full strength, the mode", "section": "Pages 25–27", "version": "1:46b63aeb22c661ff", "sourceId": "136cd389-8be9-4f12-937f-8bcbc5acf96a", "sourceType": "document"}, {"page": 28, "label": "Machine Learning — Module 5: Learning from Examples (p. 28–30)", "excerpt": "Another com plete solved example can be foun d at - https://kindsonthegenius.com/blog/how - to - build - a - decision - tree - for - classification - step - by - step - procedure - using - entrop y - and - gain/ Visit www.sharikatr.in for my notes and ppts So 𝐺𝑎𝑖𝑛 𝑆, 𝐴 1 = ES − { 𝑆 𝐴1=1 𝑆 𝐸𝑛𝑡𝑟𝑜𝑝𝑦 𝑆 𝐴1=1 + 𝑆 𝐴1=0 𝑆 𝐸𝑛𝑡𝑟𝑜𝑝𝑦 𝑆 𝐴1=0 } = 1 − 3 6 𝑋0 .9183 + 3 6 𝑋 0.9183 = 0.0817 ----- (1) DEPARTMENT OF CSE SNGCE 68 |S A2=1 |=4 Entropy(S A2=1 )= -P 1 log 2 P 1 - P 0 log 2 P 0 = − 2 4 𝑙𝑜𝑔 2 2 4 − 2 4 𝑙𝑜𝑔 2 2 4 = 1 |S A2=0 |=2 Entropy(S A1=0 )= − 1 2 𝑙𝑜𝑔 2 1 2 − 1 2 𝑙𝑜𝑔 2 1 2 = 1 DEPARTMENT OF CSE SNGCE 69 X A2 Y X1 1 1 X2 1 1 X5 1 0 X6 1 0 X A2 Y X3 0 0 X4 0 1 S A2=1 S A2=0 Visit https://www.youtube.com/c/sharikatr for my video lectures Visit www.sharikatr.in for my notes and ppts Visit www.sharikatr.in for my notes and ppts So 𝐺𝑎𝑖𝑛 𝑆, 𝐴 2 = ES − { 𝑆 𝐴2=1 𝑆 𝐸𝑛𝑡𝑟𝑜𝑝𝑦 𝑆 𝐴2=1 + 𝑆 𝐴2=0 𝑆 𝐸𝑛𝑡𝑟𝑜𝑝𝑦 𝑆 𝐴2=0 } = 1 − 4 6 𝑋 1 + 2 6 𝑋 1 = 0 ---------- (2) DEPARTMENT OF CSE SNGCE 70 From (1) and (2) We found that A1 give more information gain. So we make A1 as root node DEPARTMENT OF CSE SNGCE 71 A1 A2 1 0 A2 1 1 0 0 1 0 0 1 X A2", "section": "Pages 28–30", "version": "1:46b63aeb22c661ff", "sourceId": "136cd389-8be9-4f12-937f-8bcbc5acf96a", "sourceType": "document"}, {"page": 31, "label": "Machine Learning — Module 5: Learning from Examples (p. 31–33)", "excerpt": "From error rates to loss • So far, we have been trying to minimize error rate. This is clearly better than maximizing error rate, this is not enough, • Consider the problem of classifying email m